<PageTitle>Blazor Ramp - Accessible Blazor components</PageTitle>

<div class="landing">

    <section class="landing__hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
        <h1 id="hero-heading">Accessible Blazor components, built to WCAG from the start</h1>
        <p class="landing__lead">
            Components designed for keyboard and screen reader users first,
            with live region announcements, large touch targets and contrast-checked themes.
        </p>
        <div class="landing__actions">
            <a class="landing__btn landing__btn--primary" href="/getting-started">Get started</a>
            <a class="landing__btn landing__btn--secondary" href="/components">Components</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing__section" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
        <h2 id="install-heading">Install</h2>
        <pre class="landing__code"><code>dotnet add package BlazorRamp</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="landing__section" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
        <h2 id="features-heading">Why Blazor Ramp</h2>
        <ul class="landing__cards">
            <li>
                <h3>Tested with assistive technology</h3>
                <p>Checked with screen readers and keyboard-only navigation, not just automated tools.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h3>WCAG 2.2 focused</h3>
                <p>Target sizes, focus indicators and contrast follow the guidelines. State your level here once you can back it up.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h3>Light and dark themes</h3>
                <p>Both themes use design tokens with contrast checked for each.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h3>Any Blazor hosting model</h3>
                <p>Works with Server, WebAssembly and Auto render modes.</p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="landing__section" aria-labelledby="demo-heading">
        <h2 id="demo-heading">See it working</h2>
        <p>Replace this with one live component, such as the live region announcer.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="landing__footer">
        <a href="@GlobalValues.Web_Site_Path_GitHub_Repo">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.nuget.org/">NuGet</a>
        <span>MIT licence</span>
    </footer>

</div>